## 4) File-by-file breakdown

### Root `src/`

- `Main.java`
  - Minimal Java entry-point sanity check (`Hello, World!`).
- `EagerSingleton.java`
  - Eager singleton initialization pattern using a static final instance.
- `SortCities.java`
  - Sorting a `Map<String, Integer>` by value and key using streams.
  - Includes helpers for ascending/descending and filtering by minimum distance.

### Package `com.hybrs`

- `com/hybrs/Bank.java`
  - Constructor practice, deposit/withdraw validation, and balance management.
- `com/hybrs/GenericsTest.java`
  - Demonstrates raw `List` usage and mixed-type insertion (why generics matter).
- `com/hybrs/User.java`
  - Encapsulation with fields/getters/setters and access modifier examples.
- `com/hybrs/Test.java`
  - Marker interface example (`Serializable`), overloading, modifier checks, and quick stream snippets.

### Package `com.pattern.creational`

- `com/pattern/creational/Singleton.java`
  - Marker/interface placeholder for singleton-related pattern practice.
- `com/pattern/creational/TestProtect.java`
  - Inheritance-based access check for `protected` members across packages.

### Package `com.practice`

- `com/practice/ArrayTest.java`
  - `int[]` to `List<Integer>`, filtering evens, distinct values, squaring, sorting, frequency maps, and reverse sorting.
- `com/practice/MapFlatMapPractice.java`
  - Focused `map`/`flatMap` exercises: uppercase conversion, word counts, nested-list flattening, CSV split flattening.
- `com/practice/PartitioningPractice.java`
  - `partitioningBy` and `groupingBy` patterns for even/odd, string length, adults/minors, and grouped counting.
- `com/practice/ReductionPractice.java`
  - `reduce`, `min`, `max`, counting tasks scaffold (some TODO/incomplete methods).
- `com/practice/Practice2Java8.java`
  - Mixed Java 8 interview-style stream problems (duplicates, counts, first element, sorting, chars).
  - Several methods are intentionally TODO/incomplete for practice.
- `com/practice/Question2.java`
  - Finds odd-occurrence element using both `groupingBy` and XOR approach.
- `com/practice/ParenthesisExample.java`
  - Stack-based valid bracket/nesting checker.
- `com/practice/Test.java`
  - Sum of multiples of 3/5 using iterative and recursive methods.
- `com/practice/TreePrinter.java`
  - Recursive hierarchical tree printing from a parent->children map.
- `com/practice/ImpexCreation.java`
  - Large string preprocessing utility for formatting product codes into quoted/comma-separated output.

## 5) What kind of practice this repo is best for

- Java beginners moving from syntax to real coding patterns.
- Stream API practice for coding interviews.
- Understanding when to use `partitioningBy` vs `groupingBy`.
- Recursion and data-structure fundamentals.
- Access control behavior across packages and inheritance.

## 6) How to run examples

You can run classes individually (if they have a `main` method).

```bash
cd /Users/amit.k.bansal/Documents/TestJava
javac src/Main.java
java -cp src Main
```

Example for packaged class:

```bash
cd /Users/amit.k.bansal/Documents/TestJava
javac src/com/practice/ParenthesisExample.java
java -cp src com.practice.ParenthesisExample
```

To compile all Java files at once:

```bash
cd /Users/amit.k.bansal/Documents/TestJava
javac $(find src -name "*.java")
```

